<title>THAILAND: Bangkok Bank Q3 net profit up 9.9 pct.</title>
<headline>Bangkok Bank Q3 net profit up 9.9 pct.</headline>
<dateline>BANGKOK 1996-11-14</dateline>
<text>
<p>Audited financial results for three months ending September 30, 1996.</p>
<p>		   (in millions of baht unless stated)</p>
<p>				 Third quarter</p>
<p>    Shr (baht)		 5.11	 vs	     4.65</p>
<p>    Net		    5,115.93	 vs	 4,655.71</p>
<p>NOTES: Nine-month profits not available. Company's full name is Bangkok Bank Plc, Thailand's largest commercial bank.</p>
<p>Capital Nomura's Marshall said he expected to see some pressure on loan margins in the second quarter of 1997 as the economy bottoms out but said Bangkok Bank's size and international profile continued to offer it a competitive advantage.</p>
<p>(US$1 = 25 baht)</p>
<p>-- Bangkok newsroom (662)-2529950-3</p>
</text>
